  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "Thailand changed its currency policy, index funds were drawing money, and companies were changing leaders and products.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "The mix of assets mattered. Cash and the Treasury-bond estimate rose while many shares fell. They spread risk beyond the fortunes of individual businesses.",
    "what_faded_away": "A well-known brand and a popular theater production did not prevent losses in a company’s shares. Recent market success was not a promise of five more good years.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "The coming sequence of crises and market falls was unknown. A sensible plan still had to allow for outcomes that the starting headlines did not predict.",
